+//  and runtime are untouched.  Table syntax desugars into `makeTable` prim-apps
+//  and runtime method calls *before* type-checking, so we recover the schema by
+//  (a) reading the literal header strings + cell types of a `makeTable` call and
+//  (b) giving precise result types to the runtime table/row methods, keying off
